Z||000000||ejayerik||12-13-2001||07:04 PM||||As it stands now, the 180,000 miles on my Fiero has not damaged it that much. The engine runs good. However, having said that, it will porbably blow up in the next 20 thousand miles. (knock on wood) My question is..what is a cheap alternitive to the 2.5 4 cyl. engine or ways that I could get more out of a rebuilt one? eg. roller rockers, forged pistons, magniflux everything, ect. How about the "Duke"? I am not rich, but I would like to have the parts ready if and when it gives up the ghost.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ejayerik||12-13-2001||08:04 PM||||BTW..I have an Isuzu 5-speed trans. Anything cheap that would bolt to that?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||12-13-2001||08:53 PM||||If you have a 2.5L 4 cylinder you already have the "Duke".  With 180,000 miles you're doing real good with it.  The highest milage Fiero I've seen is 420,000 on a 4 cylinder. So you only have 240,000 miles to catch up to that coupe.<P>I don't know of any "cheap" alternatives to a replacement 4 cyl Fiero engine.   You already have the low cost version.  If you go for another Fiero 4 cyl engine as a replacement, you can rebuild it any way you want.  More HP = more $.||||reg||1
